      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to keep the grotesque hack from the original commit in one place without spilling over its implications elsewhere, just change `random_and_perf_prepare_fusion()` to do something like:\n\n    int (*fn)(unsigned int cpu);\n    fn \u003d perf_event_init_cpu;\n    fn(cpu);\n    fn \u003d random_prepare_cpu;\n    fn(cpu);\n    return 0;\n\nAnd like this you keep this all contained in one place.",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b14cfc62_cb152521",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:31:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any reason not to to just do what we did for this in android12-5.10:\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS\n        perf_event_init_cpu(cpu);\n#endif\n```",
      "parentUuid": "2723b83c_23f2ac3d",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
